## Why This Is Asked
This interview question explores cross-region, multi-tenant data routing with dynamic policy-driven enrichment, end-to-end observability, and integration of AWS data primitives beyond basic pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region routing with tenant isolation
- OPA-driven enrichment at ingestion with hot policy refresh via changelog stream
- Idempotent writes to S3 Parquet and DynamoDB
- AWS Glue catalog integration with Athena for analytics
- OpenTelemetry end-to-end tracing
- Per-tenant DLQ handling and retry strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: ingestion Lambda
async function processRecord(record, ctx) {
  const tenantId = extractTenantId(record);
  const region = extractRegion(record);
  const enriched = await enrichWithOPARules(record, tenantId);
  await writeToS3Parquet(enriched, tenantId, region);
  await writeToDynamoDB(enriched, tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design content-based routing, with strict per-record validation and multi-stream fan-out. Emphasizes end-to-end tracing, fault handling, and test strategy in a realistic, beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- Content-based routing with multiple Kinesis streams
- Lambda validation of JSON schema and required fields
- Per-record tracing with AWS X-Ray
- Parquet writing to S3 and DLQ for invalid data
- LocalStack end-to-end testing

## Code Example
